{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":30774055,"ns":0,"title":"Auslander–Buchsbaum theorem","extract":"In commutative algebra, the Auslander–Buchsbaum theorem states that regular local rings are unique factorization domains.\nThe theorem was first proved by Maurice Auslander and David Buchsbaum (1959).","description":"Algebraic theorem","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}